# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the two harnesses that build real widgets.
#
# Everything here is a library allocating at startup and keeping it for the
# life of the process: fontconfig's pattern cache, cairo's toy-font-face
# table, pango's font map, and whatever the Mesa driver decides it needs. A
# process that draws one frame and exits leaves all of it behind, and none of
# it is ours -- `composercheck' showed 43,000 allocations under ASan and not
# one frame in the tree.
#
# Suppressed by module rather than by symbol on purpose. These libraries are
# stripped on most distributions, so a symbol-based rule would match on the
# machine it was written on and silently stop matching everywhere else, which
# is the failure mode a suppression file must not have.
#
# What is deliberately NOT here: glib and gobject. They are the closest thing
# to our own code in this list -- the composer scheduler runs off a Glib
# timeout and the whole GUI is GObject underneath -- so suppressing them would
# hide the leaks most worth finding. Every trace seen so far has a fontconfig
# or cairo frame further down, and one matching frame anywhere in the stack is
# all LSan needs, so nothing is lost by leaving glib out.
#
# Wired up in scripts/CMakeLists.txt, and only when the address sanitizer is
# on, so an ordinary run carries none of this.

leak:libfontconfig.so
leak:libfreetype.so
leak:libexpat.so

leak:libcairo.so
leak:libcairo-gobject.so
leak:libpango-1.0.so
leak:libpangocairo-1.0.so
leak:libpangoft2-1.0.so
leak:libharfbuzz.so

leak:libgtk-4.so
leak:libgdk_pixbuf-2.0.so
leak:librsvg-2.so

# The GL stack the toolkit brings up to draw, which on a headless runner is
# whatever software renderer is installed.
leak:libgallium
leak:libEGL
leak:libGLX
leak:libGL.so
leak:swrast
leak:libLLVM
